    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308-a4">

                <pb facs="0418" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg310"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 910.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Royalist, at Tarawa Island</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Gilbert Group</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Tabantia, a native of Tarawa, states: About six or eight months ago, whilst
                    walking along to pick cocoanuts, Capt. Kustel came up to me and told me to go to
                    his boat. I told him I did not want to go. He caught hold of my hand and told me
                    again to go. I said, “No.” He tied his handkerchief around my wrist and pointed
                    a loaded revolver at me. I snatched it from him and ran away. He has since asked
                    me to give him back the revolver, but I would not. I have it now in my
                    possession and five cartridges which I took out of it. Mr. Walkup, the
                    missionary, told <pb facs="0419" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/> me to keep it and give
                    it to a man-of-war when one came to Tarawa. He also gave me the letter which I
                    now give you.</p>
                <p>When Capt. Kustel tried to take me to his boat Peter Grant, a trader, and Eno, a
                    native of Tahiti, were with him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tabantia</hi> (his x
                        mark).</signed><lb/>Witnesses:<lb/><signed>F. St. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">L. Luscombe</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lieutenant</hi>.</signed><lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Duncan S. O. Grant</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                            Paymaster.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Before me.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ed. H. M. Davis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Captain Her Majesty’s Ship
                            Royalist.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
